# Reminder-only beat for demo step 2: the covert channel reveal.
#
# This beat never drives protolens — it only paces the presenter and shows
# short reminders (and the byte -> ASCII table) in the script pane. The
# presenter navigates by hand. Advance each step with space or Enter.
#
# Invocation (from grehack2026.sh):
#   protolens --descriptor-set life.desc capture/000002-request.pb \
#       --script beats/smuggle

title: Finding the smuggled bits

steps:
  - text: |
      Same kind of message, but protolens now shows amber flags: fields
      that do not sit the way the schema expects.

      protoc saw nothing here — the payload is value-preserving.

      👋 Move onto a flagged field.

  - text: |
      Press `w` to open the wire level on that field.

      A VARINT is base-128: little-endian 7-bit groups, and the high bit
      of each byte is a continuation bit — 1 means "another byte follows".

      👋 Look at the continuation bits on the flagged field.

  - text: |
      The trick: a spurious continuation bit. An extra byte is appended
      whose only job is to carry one hidden bit; the decoded value does
      not change, so a schema-faithful decoder never notices.

      One hidden bit per field. Read them in order across the message.

      👋 Press space to step.

  - text: |
      The bits group into bytes, and the bytes are lowercase ASCII:

        char  dec  binary        char  dec  binary        char  dec  binary
         a     97  01100001       j    106  01101010       s    115  01110011
         b     98  01100010       k    107  01101011       t    116  01110100
         c     99  01100011       l    108  01101100       u    117  01110101
         d    100  01100100       m    109  01101101       v    118  01110110
         e    101  01100101       n    110  01101110       w    119  01110111
         f    102  01100110       o    111  01101111       x    120  01111000
         g    103  01100111       p    112  01110000       y    121  01111001
         h    104  01101000       q    113  01110001       z    122  01111010
         i    105  01101001       r    114  01110010

      👋 Press space to step.

  - text: |
      Worked example — the request side:

        01100101 01111000 01110000 ... 01101110 01110100
           e        x        p     ...    n        t      → experiment

      and the response side:

        01110111 01101000 01101111 01100001 01101101 01101001
           w        h        o        a        m        i      → whoami

      👋 Press space to step.

  - text: |
      End to end: Eve asked `whoami`, Bob's machine answered `experiment`.
      The server drives a channel hidden inside ordinary Life messages.

      👋 Type `:q` to quit protolens.
